A||N||38||Bluebottlejunky||What makes you come back to your Fiero when it give you hard times?||||4||
Z||000000||Bluebottlejunky||07-20-2001||12:20 AM||||I have been haveing lots of trouble with my Fiero this first few months I have owned it..first its running good, than its not..makes me wonder sometimes.  But for some reason this little red car just keeps draging me back to it.  I get to the point were "That's it im gunna sell that Piece of S@#!$" But then I look at it..and think how good it handles, that its something special like no other car, and its MY car I haven't put sweat and blood into it for nothing..why give up now?  Any yes you ending fixing your proublem and then later on down the road...you will have to tackle another one. This is one car that makes you work for respect. What makes you guys always come running back to your Fiero?  <P>------------------<BR>Hello, My name is Mike and I am addicted too fiero's...PLEASE dont help me.<BR>85'GT 4sp<BR>AIM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||4
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||07-20-2001||01:15 AM||||Well here's a few reasons:<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723600&p=44600649&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723600&p=44600651&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723595&p=35734848&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P>Because Fieros look soooooooo good!!!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DXR_DAD||||reg||14
Z||000002||DecadenceR||07-20-2001||01:17 AM||||Determination. I never leave a job unfinished.<BR>Pride. For all those people that call it a piece of junk.<BR>satisfaction. Seeing the job finished and knowing what i went through to get it done.||||reg||1
Z||000003||AkursedX||07-20-2001||01:33 AM||||I think it's because it's MY car.  I bought it with all of my money, I did all of my own work to it, so now when something breaks down (Like it has alot lately!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> )  I feel a need to make it run again.<P>Plus it's just too damn pretty!!!!!  I can't stay mad at it.  Kinda like a puppy after it chews on the furniture  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||GTMike||07-20-2001||01:41 AM||||have you ever own an old jeep.  thats all i have had for the last 6 years.   and those things break all the time.  and i was constantly upgrading to new parts.    so a fiero is no big deal to me.  i just pulled off my egr tube and jb welded it and i'll hvae it back in in the morning.  check out my post and pix in the tech  section.   ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Bluebottlejunky||07-20-2001||01:42 AM||||YA, dont think i could give up on my girl!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cheever2||07-20-2001||02:24 AM||||I just figure any other car would do almost the same thing.  A new car would have enormous payments, a used car would have repair costs too.  <P>But these are different and unique.  They aren't common anymore.  I have always avoided what everybody else was doing, and Fieros fit into that very well.<BR>||||reg||1
