Z||000020||dlancer407||07-20-2001||04:12 PM||||I think any car that is 13years old and older is going to break down from time to time. I have not had my Fiero very long and I have not had any real problems yet. I have owned a 1987 Shelby Lancer in the past that I sold to my son last year.I bought that car with only 62,000 miles on it and I loved that car. I was constantly putting money into that car. I replaced many parts including the engine in that car, but I still could not bring myself to sell it. I finally sold it to my son after much begging on his part. He is still putting money into that car ( AN ALTERNATOR JUST LAST WEEK ). He loves that car as much as I did. When you are driving a car as rare as our Fiero's  or in my son's case a numbered SHELBY car you tend to overlook there sometimes many problems in exchange for there uniqueness and rarity. ||||reg||6
