Z||000022||Fformula88||07-20-2001||10:22 PM||||I have many times pondered the thought of selling it.  Then I realize I will never find a car I absolutely love to drive as much as this one without spending big money on it.  I have owned my Fiero for a little over 4 years now, and this is the first summer it has run well enough to drive it much.  I have been replacing, and troubleshooting numerous engine problems the last three years.  Yet, when I have been able to drive it, it reminds me how much I love driving it.  I own a 97 Ford Probe as a daily driver, and love it too.  But its just not as much fun as the Fiero to drive although it performs nearly as well (its a 4-banger and not as fast).<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000023||AusFiero||07-20-2001||11:06 PM||||Hmmm interesting question. I think I just keep coming back to mine and look at it and think what a sweet little machine. I am so lucky to have a car like this that no one around here has. <P>I actually went out looking for a 1965 Mustang convertible when I bought my Fiero. Things changed once I drove my little baby. I figured a 65 Mustang is gunna be just like driving a 65 Falcon with a different body, besides the obvious appealling look. Looks nice but hey I live in an area full of windy mountain and coastal roads. The Fiero was a sure thing once I drove it.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000024||LZeitgeist||07-21-2001||12:37 PM||||I keep coming back to my Fiero because I'm too damn lazy to walk to work. <P><BR>Also, in 15+ years of owning cars, there's only about three years in there where I *didn't* own a Fiero. From the first time I sat in my first one at the used car dealership before I bought it, the damn thing fit my 6'-2", tall, lanky-ass frame like a frickin' glove. I slipped into it, slid the seat back all the way, adjusted the seat back angle a bit, and every control fell immediately to my fingertips. <P>The Fiero fits the way I'm built, the things I like, and the way I drive like no other car I've ever been in in my life. <P>I'll most likely have a Fiero to drive until I'm dead. Hell, I'll probably die in a wreck while I'm *in* my Fiero.<P>You gotta go sometime - might as well go doing something you love. Hopefully, that won't be for a long time yet, though. ||||reg||1
Z||000025||jake1852||07-21-2001||01:16 PM||||you know, i thought i was the only one that goes through this ****  with my car. i hate the fu*king thing, and then when i look out my window and see it, i love it. i look at the prices for various mods, and i hate my car...then i drive it like it is, and love it again... a really fuc*ed up relationship here..||||reg||1
