Z||000037||87GTBro||07-25-2001||01:25 PM||||I like being different.  I like driving a car that nobody else drives.  (Well, at least in my area)  I live in a city of 50,000.  Do you know how many GT's there are in my town?<P>3<P>I own 2 of them and my brother owns the other one!  I could drive a brand new rustang or firethebird, but every punk kid in town owns a TA or a rustang.<P>I want to be different.  And there is a sense of satisfaction when you pass people on the road and look in the rear view mirror to see them make a double-take.  Never seen anyone do that to a rustang before!<P>Last week I saw a GT the only other GT around here for sale.  I bought it.  Partly because I wanted to retain my uniqueness, and partly because I can use the car for future projects.  <P>I am crazy about these cars...  Overall, it is much cheaper to maintain these cars than to have a $300/mo car payment.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierogroupshot1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000038||fierobaby||07-25-2001||01:35 PM||||so I sat here thinking geez....what does make me come back to my car...it costs me tons of money and it can be the biggest pain in the butt! but its a really pretty car and it catches peoples eyes... plus it makes my brother mad that I got a great car as my first car. HE always calls it a peice of $%&T but he has a dodge daytona A Jeep cheeroke and a Ford Escort the escort doesn't even run the jeep is UGLY and the DAYTON! we won't touch that one! but my car...its pretty..its special...something you don't see all the time||||reg||1
